  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Stat Count-up With Bars\n\nA muted label and a giant figure counting up in tight black type with a unit under it, then a bar chart whose bars grow while their values count (the last one in the accent colour, the rest in light grey), then a percent ring that draws itself with its figure and a few words beside it. White page.\n\nCategory: commerce. Length: 9 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A business milestone, a channel's numbers or a data-led lesson with one headline figure, a short trend and one percentage.\n- Figures that should be read in order: total first, trend second, share last.\n\nAvoid when:\n- Only one number: use a plain counter block.\n- More than six data points or exact axes: use a real chart block.\n- Several milestones as a list: use milestone-counter-list.\n\nVariables:\n- label (string): Label, default \"Bulan ini kami mencuci\"\n- number (number, 0-999999999): Big number, default 12000\n- number_suffix (string): Number suffix, default \"+\"\n- unit (string): Unit, default \"kg pakaian pelanggan\"\n- bars (string): Bars, default \"Jul|4,1\\nAgu|6,3\\nSep|8,6\\nOkt|12\"\n- bar_suffix (string): Bar value suffix, default \"t\"\n- percent (number, 0-100): Percent, default 98\n- percent_label (string): Percent label, default \"pelanggan puas dan langganan lagi\"\n- bg_color (color): Background, default \"#ffffff\"\n- accent_color (color): Accent, default \"#2563eb\"\n- text_color (color): Text colour, default \"#0a0a0a\"\n- muted_color (color): Muted colour, default \"#737373\"\n- transparent (boolean): Transparent, default false\n\nSource: Mosio original. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
